WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.980
Your first business sheet: clean records and first formulas.

2
00:00:04.330 --> 00:00:09.280
This is the video for Module 1 of Excel and Google Sheets for Small Business.

3
00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:19.270
Many of us keep records in an exercise book or in our heads. That works until you need a quick answer, like how much did I sell last month?

4
00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:33.020
A spreadsheet is a grid on your phone or computer that stores your records and does the calculations for you. Excel and Google Sheets work almost the same, so pick the one you can open most easily.

5
00:00:34.270 --> 00:00:38.840
Change one number, and every total that depends on it updates by itself.

6
00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:42.410
And your file will be backed up and protected.

7
00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:47.930
First, a few words. A column runs up and down, named by a letter.

8
00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:51.700
A row runs across, named by a number.

9
00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:58.220
A cell is one box where they meet, named column letter then row number, so C5.

10
00:00:59.470 --> 00:01:04.990
A range is a block of cells. C2 colon C10 means C2 down to C10.

11
00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:14.710
The formula bar, marked f x, shows what is really inside a cell. The cell shows the answer, the formula bar shows the formula.

12
00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:20.570
Step 1. Open Google Sheets or Excel and create a new blank file.

13
00:01:21.820 --> 00:01:26.730
Step 2. Give the file a clear name, for example your business name and the year.

14
00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:33.550
Step 3. Rename the first tab to Sales. On a phone, tap the tab and choose Rename.

15
00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:40.450
Step 4. In row 1, type the headings. Date, Item, Quantity, Unit price, and Amount.

16
00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:51.150
Step 5. Type one sale in row 2. In cell E2, type equals C2 star D2, and press Enter. The star means multiply.

17
00:01:52.400 --> 00:02:00.270
Remember this rule. Every formula starts with an equals sign. Without it, the spreadsheet treats what you type as plain text.

18
00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:10.030
Here is a worked example. Ngozi runs a small provisions shop in Enugu and wants to stop adding up sales on a calculator at night.

19
00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:19.030
She sells 2 cartons of noodles at 9500, so equals C2 star D2 gives 19000.

20
00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:30.020
3 bottles of groundnut oil at 3200 give 9600. 6 bars of soap at 700 give 4200.

21
00:02:31.270 --> 00:02:36.760
In E5 she adds them up. The day's total is 32800 naira.

22
00:02:37.110 --> 00:02:48.410
Later she corrects the soap price to 750. E4 becomes 4500 and the total 33100, without her doing anything else.

23
00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:58.690
A spreadsheet can only calculate what it understands. Type 5000 as a plain number, then let formatting add the naira sign and the commas.

24
00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:05.650
Keep one row for each sale or expense, one column for each detail, and headings in row 1 only.

25
00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:16.240
This is the common mistake. If you type N5000 or 5k, the sheet sees words, not a number, and your totals will quietly be wrong.

26
00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:22.930
Quick check. Numbers sit on the right of the cell, text on the left. If an amount sits on the left, retype it.

27
00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:36.060
Now, functions. These are ready-made calculations with names. Bisi sells rice and stew in Ibadan, and types her daily takings for 6 days in cells B2 to B7.

28
00:03:37.310 --> 00:03:42.350
SUM adds the whole range. Her week comes to 97000 naira.

29
00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:52.220
MIN finds her worst day, 8000 on Tuesday. MAX finds her best day, 30500 on Saturday.

30
00:03:52.570 --> 00:04:01.480
AVERAGE counts zeros but ignores empty cells. So she leaves Sunday blank, when she is closed, and her average reflects trading days only.

31
00:04:02.730 --> 00:04:11.240
Your records are money, so protect them. Save online. A phone that is stolen or dropped in water should not take your records with it.

32
00:04:12.490 --> 00:04:17.700
Use version history to go back to an earlier copy, and download a backup once a month.

33
00:04:18.950 --> 00:04:30.380
And never open spreadsheet attachments from strangers that ask you to Enable Macros to see an invoice or payment alert. That is a common way to install harmful software.

34
00:04:31.630 --> 00:04:38.550
To remember. Cells are named column letter, then row number. Type facts once and let formulas do the maths.

35
00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:47.790
Type plain numbers, with no N and no k. Use SUM, AVERAGE, MIN and MAX. And keep your file saved online and safe from scams.

36
00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:57.020
Now it is your turn. Set up your own Sales sheet with three real sales, clean and format it, then work out your week in numbers.

37
00:04:57.370 --> 00:04:59.310
Continue with the lessons below.
